{"id":"mahabharata-7-100","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":100,"title":"शततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 100 · Duryodhana rouses his army","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks whether his army had no great warriors left to stop Satyaki. Duryodhana urges his chiefs to prevent Satyaki and Arjuna from joining, and the Pandava army, led by Satyaki, presses forward like a lotus-pond overrun by an elephant.","kn":"ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯನ್ನು ತಡೆಯಲು ತನ್ನ ಸೈನ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಮಹಾರಥರೇ ಇರಲಿಲ್ಲವೇ ಎಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ-ಅರ್ಜುನರು ಸೇರದಂತೆ ತಡೆಯಲು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ತನ್ನ ಮುಖ್ಯರನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಮುಂದೆ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಆನೆ ತುಳಿದ ಕಮಲ ಸರೋವರದಂತೆ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि क्या उनकी सेना में सात्यकि को रोकने वाला कोई महारथी न बचा। दुर्योधन अपने प्रमुखों को सात्यकि और अर्जुन के मिलन को रोकने के लिए प्रेरित करता है, और सात्यकि के नेतृत्व में पाण्डव सेना आगे बढ़ती है।","te":"సాత్యకిని ఆపడానికి తన సేనలో మహారథులే లేరా అని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. సాత్యకి, అర్జునుడు కలవకుండా ఆపమని దుర్యోధనుడు తన నాయకులను పురికొల్పుతాడు; సాత్యకి నాయకత్వంలో పాండవసేన ముందుకు సాగుతుంది.","ta":"சாத்யகியைத் தடுக்கக் கூடிய பெருந்தேர்வீரர் தன் படையில் இல்லையா என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். சாத்யகியும் அர்ஜுனனும் சேராமல் தடுக்கத் துரியோதனன் தன் தலைவர்களைத் தூண்ட, சாத்யகி தலைமையில் பாண்டவப் படை முன்னேறுகிறது.","ml":"സാത്യകിയെ തടയാൻ തന്റെ സേനയിൽ മഹാവീരന്മാർ ഇനിയില്ലേ എന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. സാത്യകിയെയും അർജുനനെയും ഒന്നിക്കാൻ അനുവദിക്കരുതെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനൻ നേതാക്കളോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; ആനയാൽ ചവിട്ടിമെതിക്കപ്പെട്ട താമരക്കുളംപോലെ, സാത്യകി നയിക്കുന്ന പാണ്ഡവ സേന മുന്നോട്ടു കുതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.100; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"किं तस्यां मम सेनायां नासन्केचिन्महारथाः ।\nये तथा सात्यकिं यान्तं नैवाघ्नन्नाप्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Were there no great chariot-warriors left in my army, that none of them struck down Satyaki as he passed, or even stopped him?"}},{"n":2,"text":"एको हि समरे कर्म कृतवान्सत्यविक्रमः ।\nशक्रतुल्यबलो युद्धे महेन्द्रो दानवेष्विव ॥","meaning":{"en":"For that one man, true in valor, did such deeds in battle, with strength like Indra's, as great Indra did among the Danavas."}},{"n":3,"text":"अथ वा शून्यमासीत्तद्येन यातः स सात्यकिः ।\nएको वै बहुलाः सेनाः प्रमृद्नन्पुरुषर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or else was the host empty where Satyaki went, that he, that best of men, crushed so many divisions alone?"}},{"n":4,"text":"कथं च युध्यमानानामपक्रान्तो महात्मनाम् ।\nएको बहूनां शैनेयस्तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me, Sanjaya, how Shini's descendant alone slipped away from so many great-souled men who were fighting."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"राजन्सेनासमुद्योगो रथनागाश्वपत्तिमान् ।\nतुमुलस्तव सैन्यानां युगान्तसदृशोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, the stir of your army, with its chariots, elephants, horses and foot soldiers, became as tumultuous as the end of an age."}},{"n":6,"text":"आह्णिकेषु समूहेषु तव सैन्यस्य मानद ।\nनास्ति लोके समः कश्चित्समूह इति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O giver of honor, I think there is no gathering in the world like your army's daily gatherings."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत्र देवाः स्म भाषन्ते चारणाश्च समागताः ।\nएतदन्ताः समूहा वै भविष्यन्ति महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the gods and the charanas who had assembled said, \"Such gatherings will end with this one on earth.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"न चैव तादृशः कश्चिद्व्यूह आसीद्विशां पते ।\nयादृग्जयद्रथवधे द्रोणेन विहितोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And no battle array, lord of the people, was ever like the one Drona devised for the slaying of Jayadratha."}},{"n":9,"text":"चण्डवाताभिपन्नानां समुद्राणामिव स्वनः ।\nरणेऽभवद्बलौघानामन्योन्यमभिधावताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The roar of the surging hosts rushing at one another in battle was like the sound of oceans struck by a fierce gale."}},{"n":10,"text":"पार्थिवानां समेतानां बहून्यासन्नरोत्तम ।\nत्वद्बले पाण्डवानां च सहस्राणि शतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the kings assembled there were many thousands and hundreds in your force and among the Pandavas, best of men."}},{"n":11,"text":"संरब्धानां प्रवीराणां समरे दृढकर्मणाम् ।\nतत्रासीत्सुमहाञ्शब्दस्तुमुलो लोमहर्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A mighty, tumultuous, hair-raising noise rose from those furious heroes of firm deeds in the fight."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथाक्रन्दद्भीमसेनो धृष्टद्युम्नश्च मारिष ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च धर्मराजश्च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhimasena and Dhrishtadyumna cried out, sir, and Nakula, Sahadeva and Yudhishthira, the Pandava king of dharma."}},{"n":13,"text":"आगच्छत प्रहरत बलवत्परिधावत ।\nप्रविष्टावरिसेनां हि वीरौ माधवपाण्डवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Come, strike, charge hard! The two heroes, Krishna and Arjuna, have entered the enemy host.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"यथा सुखेन गच्छेतां जयद्रथवधं प्रति ।\nतथा प्रकुरुत क्षिप्रमिति सैन्यान्यचोदयत् ।\nतयोरभावे कुरवः कृतार्थाः स्युर्वयं जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Act quickly so that they may go easily to the slaying of Jayadratha.\" So he urged the troops, adding, \"Without those two the Kurus would be fulfilled and we defeated.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"ते यूयं सहिता भूत्वा तूर्णमेव बलार्णवम् ।\nक्षोभयध्वं महावेगाः पवनाः सागरं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So band together and swiftly churn this ocean of an army with great force, as winds churn the sea.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"भीमसेनेन ते राजन्पाञ्चाल्येन च चोदिताः ।\nआजघ्नुः कौरवान्संख्ये त्यक्त्वासूनात्मनः प्रियान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on by Bhimasena and the Panchala prince, O king, they struck the Kauravas in battle, giving up their own dear lives."}},{"n":17,"text":"इच्छन्तो निधनं युद्धे शस्त्रैरुत्तमतेजसः ।\nस्वर्गार्थं मित्रकार्यार्थं नाभ्यरक्षन्त जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men of supreme energy, seeking death in battle by weapons for the sake of heaven and for their friends' cause, did not guard their lives."}},{"n":18,"text":"तथैव तावका राजन्प्रार्थयन्तो महद्यशः ।\nआर्यां युद्धे मतिं कृत्वा युद्धायैवोपतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your men likewise, O king, seeking great fame and setting their minds on the noble way of battle, stood ready to fight."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु तुमुले युद्धे वर्तमाने महाभये ।\nहत्वा सर्वाणि सैन्यानि प्रायात्सात्यकिरर्जुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that tumultuous, terrible battle went on, Satyaki, having slain all the divisions, went on toward Arjuna."}},{"n":20,"text":"कवचानां प्रभास्तत्र सूर्यरश्मिविचित्रिताः ।\nदृष्टीः संख्ये सैनिकानां प्रतिजघ्नुः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the gleam of the armor, varied like sunbeams, struck back at the eyes of the soldiers on every side."}},{"n":21,"text":"तथा प्रयतमानेषु पाण्डवेयेषु निर्भयः ।\nदुर्योधनो महाराज व्यगाहत महद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Pandavas were thus exerting themselves, Duryodhana, fearless, O great king, plunged into their great force."}},{"n":22,"text":"स संनिपातस्तुमुलस्तेषां तस्य च भारत ।\nअभवत्सर्वसैन्यानामभावकरणो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The clash between them and him, O Bharata, was tumultuous and vast, bringing about the ruin of all the armies."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"तथा गतेषु सैन्येषु तथा कृच्छ्रगतः स्वयम् ।\nकच्चिद्दुर्योधनः सूत नाकार्षीत्पृष्ठतो रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the armies had fared so, and he himself in such straits, Sanjaya, did Duryodhana never turn his back on the fight?"}},{"n":24,"text":"एकस्य च बहूनां च संनिपातो महाहवे ।\nविशेषतो नृपतिना विषमः प्रतिभाति मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"A clash of one against many in a great battle seems to me uneven, especially when the one is a king."}},{"n":25,"text":"सोऽत्यन्तसुखसंवृद्धो लक्ष्म्या लोकस्य चेश्वरः ।\nएको बहून्समासाद्य कच्चिन्नासीत्पराङ्मुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was raised in utmost comfort, the master of the world with its prosperity; did he, one man against many, never turn away?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"राजन्संग्राममाश्चर्यं तव पुत्रस्य भारत ।\nएकस्य च बहूनां च शृणुष्व गदतोऽद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, hear the marvelous battle of your son, the astonishing fight of one against many, O Bharata."}},{"n":27,"text":"दुर्योधनेन सहसा पाण्डवी पृतना रणे ।\nनलिनी द्विरदेनेव समन्ताद्विप्रलोडिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suddenly Duryodhana in the fight tossed the Pandava host about on all sides, as an elephant tosses a lotus pond."}},{"n":28,"text":"तथा सेनां कृतां दृष्ट्वा तव पुत्रेण कौरव ।\nभीमसेनपुरोगास्तं पाञ्चालाः समुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the army so treated by your son, O Kaurava, the Panchalas with Bhimasena at their head rushed at him."}},{"n":29,"text":"स भीमसेनं दशभिर्माद्रीपुत्रौ त्रिभिस्त्रिभिः ।\nविराटद्रुपदौ षड्भिः शतेन च शिखण्डिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Bhimasena with ten arrows, the two sons of Madri with three each, Virata and Drupada with six each, and Shikhandin with a hundred."}},{"n":30,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नं च विंशत्या धर्मपुत्रं च सप्तभिः ।\nकेकयान्दशभिर्विद्ध्वा द्रौपदेयांस्त्रिभिस्त्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Dhrishtadyumna with twenty and the son of Dharma with seven, the Kekayas with ten, and the sons of Draupadi with three each."}},{"n":31,"text":"शतशश्चापरान्योधान्सद्विपांश्च रथान्रणे ।\nशरैरवचकर्तोग्रैः क्रुद्धोऽन्तक इव प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And he cut down hundreds of other warriors, with elephants and chariots, in battle with fierce arrows, like angry Death among creatures."}},{"n":32,"text":"न संदधन्विमुञ्चन्वा मण्डलीकृतकार्मुकः ।\nअदृश्यत रिपून्निघ्नञ्शिक्षयास्त्रबलेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his bow drawn into a circle he was not seen fitting or loosing arrows, yet he kept slaying foes by his skill and the power of his weapons."}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्य तान्निघ्नतः शत्रून्हेमपृष्ठं महद्धनुः ।\nभल्लाभ्यां पाण्डवो ज्येष्ठस्त्रिधा चिच्छेद मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he slaughtered those enemies, O sir, the eldest Pandava cut his great gold-backed bow in three with two broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":34,"text":"विव्याध चैनं बहुभिः सम्यगस्तैः शितैः शरैः ।\nवर्माण्याशु समासाद्य ते भग्नाः क्षितिमाविशन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also pierced him with many sharp, well-aimed arrows; they reached his armor quickly, broke, and fell to the ground."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततः प्रमुदिताः पार्थाः परिवव्रुर्युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nयथा वृत्रवधे देवा मुदा शक्रं महर्षिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the delighted sons of Pritha gathered around Yudhishthira, as the gods with great sages gathered in joy around Shakra at the slaying of Vritra."}},{"n":36,"text":"अथ दुर्योधनो राजा दृढमादाय कार्मुकम् ।\nतिष्ठ तिष्ठेति राजानं ब्रुवन्पाण्डवमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, taking a firm bow, advanced on the Pandava king, saying, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":37,"text":"तं तथा वादिनं राजंस्तव पुत्रं महारथम् ।\nप्रत्युद्ययुः प्रमुदिताः पाञ्चाला जयगृद्धिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As your son, the great chariot-warrior, spoke so, O king, the Panchalas, eager for victory, rushed gladly to meet him."}},{"n":38,"text":"तान्द्रोणः प्रतिजग्राह परीप्सन्युधि पाण्डवम् ।\nचण्डवातोद्धुतान्मेघान्सजलानचलो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona received them, wishing to seize the Pandava in the fight, as a mountain receives water-laden clouds driven by a fierce wind."}},{"n":39,"text":"तत्र राजन्महानासीत्संग्रामो भूरिवर्धनः ।\nरुद्रस्याक्रीडसंकाशः संहारः सर्वदेहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O king, a mighty battle took place, swelling in force, like Rudra's sport, the destruction of all embodied beings."}}]}]}